From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 05 May 2026 16:40:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: allow SW fast path when WED is disabled

mt7996_net_fill_forward_path() currently returns -ENODEV when neither
WED nor NPU is active, which kills net_fill_forward_path() at the wifi
hop. With WED off this prevents nft_flow_offload and xt_FLOWOFFLOAD
from learning the eth->wifi bridged flow, so every packet traverses
the full bridge ingress and conntrack path on the host CPU.

The trailing block already gracefully falls back to band_idx when WED
and NPU are inactive, so the early return is the only barrier. Drop
it and let the function fill in path->type and path->dev so the SW
flow offload path can stitch the bridge ports together.

Based on Peter Chiu's MTK feed patch
0024-mtk-mt76-mt7996-support-sw-fast-path-when-wed-is-dis.patch,
adapted for this tree where path->type is already set unconditionally.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |    4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -2583,10 +2583,6 @@ mt7996_net_fill_forward_path(struct ieee
 	     (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76) && msta_link->wcid.phy_idx == MT_BAND1)))
 		wed = &dev->mt76.mmio.wed_hif2;
 
-	if (!mtk_wed_device_active(wed) &&
-	    !mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
-		return -ENODEV;
-
 	path->type = DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA;
 	path->dev = ctx->dev;
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
